// globals.marco — global commands ported from MacroMarco's globals module,
// driven by hotkey events. Run as a persistent server and pipe Hotkeys events
// (e.g. from the AHK UI capturing the backtick leader key) to its stdin:
//
//   marco serve --host windows programs/globals.marco
//   ...then feed lines like: {"feed":"Hotkeys","event":"E"}
//
// Each command is one action; the host performs the real key/mouse work.

use os.

// Inbound global-hotkey events (host -> Marco). A host that captures the
// backtick leader key writes these as {"feed":"Hotkeys","event":"E"} lines.
the Hotkeys is a feed of any.

the Globals is an actor.

this can PressE.
this's PressE does...
    do OS's Key with "e".
    this is ok!

this can ClickHere.
this's ClickHere does...
    do OS's Click.
    this is ok!

this can Greet.
this's Greet does...
    do OS's Type with "gg".
    do OS's Key with "enter".
    this is ok!

// Leader-key command routing: each hotkey event runs one command.
when Hotkeys reads E?
    do Globals's PressE...
        when ok?
            log "pressed e".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads Click?
    do Globals's ClickHere...
        when ok?
            log "clicked".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads Greet?
    do Globals's Greet...
        when ok?
            log "greeted".
        or?
            log that's error.

the App is a script.
log "globals ready".
